WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.011
Why repeat the same cleaning twice?

2
00:00:03.011 --> 00:00:08.171
In this lesson, you will learn to replace several values in a text column,

3
00:00:08.171 --> 00:00:13.331
find those steps in the Advanced Editor, and paste them into another query, fixing

4
00:00:13.331 --> 00:00:16.280
the errors along the way. Let's work smarter!

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:21.749
Here we have two copies of the Financial Sample.

6
00:00:21.749 --> 00:00:26.480
The second copy, Financial Sample two, has a few cleaning steps already.

7
00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.667
In the Product column, I replace product names with short labels.

8
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:09.552
Right click a value and choose Replace Values.

9
00:01:09.552 --> 00:01:13.880
Type the value to find, and the value to replace it with.

10
00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.780
I replace three products, one by one.

11
00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:43.420
Each replacement becomes its own step:

12
00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:47.380
Replaced Value, Replaced Value one, and Replaced Value two.

13
00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.447
Now open the Advanced Editor.

14
00:02:02.447 --> 00:02:05.593
Here are the three replace steps, written in M.

15
00:02:05.593 --> 00:02:07.340
I select and copy them.

16
00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:29.488
In the other query, I open the Advanced Editor and paste the lines. Notice the error: Token comma expected.

17
00:02:29.488 --> 00:02:33.060
The new lines must connect to the steps around them.

18
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.975
Each step must refer to the step before it by name, and every line

19
00:02:51.975 --> 00:02:55.640
needs a comma at the end, except the last one before in.

20
00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.379
Another message:

21
00:03:10.379 --> 00:03:12.076
a comma cannot precede in.

22
00:03:12.076 --> 00:03:16.149
So I remove the extra comma, and the code is valid again.

23
00:03:16.149 --> 00:03:19.882
Read each message carefully, and fix one thing at a time.

24
00:03:19.882 --> 00:03:21.240
You can do it!

